WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.079
It was European Commission President Jean-Claude Juncker's fourth 

00:00:03.079 --> 00:00:06.479
and last State of the Union address at the European Parliament. 

00:00:06.479 --> 00:00:12.039
I would like next year's elections to be a landmark of European democracy. 

00:00:12.039 --> 00:00:14.519
With eight months before the European elections, 

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:17.839
the debate was an opportunity to sketch an ambitious path

00:00:17.839 --> 00:00:20.159
 for the future of the EU of 27.

00:00:20.159 --> 00:00:23.159
  The European Parliament wants, more than ever, to be at the heart of democracy. 

00:00:23.159 --> 00:00:27.239
I thank you for the initiatives to make our European elections safe. 

00:00:27.239 --> 00:00:31.879
Not trolls, not fake news, not Cambridge Analytica will decide, the people will decide. 

00:00:31.879 --> 00:00:34.600
I want to ask the Commission in the coming months

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.280
 to introduce a package of proposals to protect our elections

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:42.639
 against foreign meddling. 

00:00:42.639 --> 00:00:46.600
Juncker stressed the need for unity in the face of rising populism.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.479
This belief that 'united we stand taller' is the very essence 

00:00:50.479 --> 00:00:54.239
of what it means to be part of the European Union. 

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:58.879
Members looked back on Juncker's achievements and called for action on migration, 

00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:00.800
climate change and the economy.

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.400
 We have to open legal ways for migration. 

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:07.879
It's a scandal what we witnessed again this summer in the Mediterranean. 

00:01:07.879 --> 00:01:10.639
Climate change is happening, it's happening now. 

00:01:10.639 --> 00:01:14.639
The good news about climate change is that we know what to do.

00:01:14.639 --> 00:01:18.519
 The bad news is that we don't do it. 

00:01:18.519 --> 00:01:23.759
We have to admit that 10 years after the financial crisis, 

00:01:23.759 --> 00:01:29.920
the previous level of prosperity has not been re-established in many countries. 

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:32.800
Others touched upon the current divisions in Europe. 

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.519
The number of people who are deeply dissatisfied 

00:01:37.519 --> 00:01:40.079
with the European project is increasing. 

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:43.439
You made no acknowledgement of the populist revolt

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:47.239
 that is sweeping through virtually every single member state. 

00:01:47.239 --> 00:01:53.879
Your Commission's action is opaque, anti-democratic and harsh. 

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:57.560
Juncker stressed the need to turn Europe into a greater global player

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:01.639
 on the world stage – protecting the Union for the generations to come.

